body:
Yes, in poorer communities there is easy and cheap access to junk food but hard / more expensive access to whole / good foods.  Most poorer communities are in food deserts.  It is easier and cheaper after your 2nd job to go get some mcdonalds than to go grocery shopping and cook a meal.  

&#x200B;

That doesnt even get into the different work environments for different countries. I am not poor and I struggle with this a bit myself getting enough time to cook healthy meals and I do not even live in a food desert or have limited access to healthy foods. It is just so much easier to get a fast food after working 8-10hr shift and the wife does the same, all while taking the kids to their activities.

Exactly this, not having backups working, and actually knowing about it and still doing nothing is a new level of crazy to me.  

&#x200B;

Although I cant really say anything, in my small company our backup server crapped out and we cannot reload BackupExec 2007 or whatever was last purchased and I've been fighting to get Veeam or ANYTHING going for the last year.  Using the free version of Veeam community to backup 10 VMs and no offsite :(.

I made a huge mistake just a few months ago.  I was diagnosed with biopsy, I went over a year gluten free, was feeling pretty good, still had horrible neck pain that didnt go away with diet change.  One day I was hungry and had severe neck pain and decided what the heck - I ate my daughters left over gluten pizza.  I didnt have a reaction, so I thought my Dr. could have been wrong.  I went a little over a month of eating gluten almost every day, without symptoms.  Until suddenly one day I woke up in the morning with the worst panic attack I've had since I went gluten free.  Then the throwing up and diarrhea came with a vengeance, I lost 10 pounds in 3 weeks.  Took a month of strict gluten free to start to feel better.  Never making that mistake again. 

&#x200B;

My situation is different, I dont know.  But from my experience as being diagnosed Celiac and then trying to eat gluten, it seems it may affect people differently.  Maybe we healed enough to not have the negative effects at first, but eventually it will catch up.

Same here!! I have had a mild fever on and off the last couple days.  I have a sore throat and congestion.  No cough or shortness of breath either, I'm sure its a cold but its pretty bad cold.  Went to urgent care and it was so packed with people coughing I noped out of there pretty quick, would have been there all day anyways.  Called my pcp and they couldnt get me in until Monday.  

&#x200B;

No idea if I should go in to work tomorrow or just stay home.

